{
  "description": "The PROXY protocol version 2 header at the start of a bound data connection, as a gateway reads it, RELAY-v0.md section 4.6. Each case: everything the gateway receives on the connection, in hex, up to the end of the stream (a header that is cut off is never completed), and the decision. accepted: the gateway uses the source address and port and has consumed that many bytes, and the bytes after them are the agent's and stay unread. refused: the gateway closes the connection. either: the source address is one that Section 4.6 does not name and that is not globally reachable; a gateway may accept it, with the source and the consumed bytes the case gives, or refuse it. The destination address and port are ignored, whatever they are. Generated with go run ./tools/vectors relay-proxy.",
  "cases": [
    {"id":"x01","section":"4.6","hex":"0d0a0d0a000d0a515549540a2111000c5db8d822c0000201c93a01bb","expected":"accepted","source":{"address":"93.184.216.34","port":51514},"consumed":28,"why":"an IPv4 agent, the form of section 4.6"},
